# Git GUESSES whether a file is text, and on Windows it rewrites the line endings of
# anything it decides is. These formats are binary, and a single CRLF substitution
# inside one is a corrupt file that still looks perfectly committed:
#
#   *.stl   32,532 NUL bytes in one sample -- raw floats
#   *.3mf   a zip, and its compressed streams contain literal CRLF byte pairs
#
# The guess is right today, but it is re-made on every clone, on machines whose
# core.autocrlf we do not control. The printable output IS this repo, so pin it.
#
# Deliberately NOT listed: *.step and the slicer *.config files. STEP is an ASCII
# format and both are genuinely text, currently stored with CRLF. Marking them binary
# -- or switching the repo to `* text=auto` -- rewrites content this change has no
# business touching.

*.3mf   binary
*.stl   binary
*.zip   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
